# CODEOWNERS — gatekeeper ownership of the Vibe-IC plugin tree
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This file routes mandatory review of every change touching the plugin (and
# the governance machinery that gates it) to the GATEKEEPER identity — the
# single role permitted to land code on `main` (see
# vibe-ic-marketplace/plugins/vibe-ic/agents/gatekeeper-agent.md and
# tools/setup_branch_protection.sh, which enables "Require review from Code
# Owners" + the native merge queue).
#
# PLACEHOLDER: `@vibeic/gatekeeper` is a stand-in team handle. The repository
# owner MUST replace it with the real GitHub team or bot/app that runs the
# gatekeeper-loop (e.g. `@vibeic/gatekeeper-bot` or a specific machine user)
# BEFORE enabling branch protection — an unresolved CODEOWNERS handle silently
# disables the Code-Owners review requirement instead of blocking the merge.
#
# Ordering note: GitHub uses the LAST matching pattern, so the broad plugin
# rule comes first and the narrower governance/CI rules come after it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The whole plugin tree (programs, skills, commands, agents, MCP server).
/vibe-ic-marketplace/plugins/vibe-ic/                @vibeic/gatekeeper

# The marketplace manifest + version source of truth.
/vibe-ic-marketplace/.claude-plugin/                 @vibeic/gatekeeper

# The governance / CI machinery that enforces the landing gate. Changing these
# is changing the gate itself — it must also go through the gatekeeper, AND the
# gatekeeper routes its OWN changes here through a second reviewer
# (who-gates-the-gatekeeper; see gatekeeper-agent.md).
/.github/workflows/gatekeeper-ci.yml                 @vibeic/gatekeeper
/.github/CODEOWNERS                                  @vibeic/gatekeeper
/tools/setup_branch_protection.sh                    @vibeic/gatekeeper
